cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  LieSeries: Lie series in generalized Hall bases of the
  free Lie algebra on two generators
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it as below.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Murua
    given-names: Ander
    affiliation: University of the Basque Country (UPV/EHU)
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3430-9642'
abstract: >-
  A Wolfram Language (Mathematica) package for computing
  with truncated Lie series in the free Lie algebra on two
  generators, expressed in generalized Hall bases in the
  sense of Viennot (Hall-type, Lyndon and other built-in
  orders). It provides Lie brackets with symbolic
  coefficients, Hall coefficients, substitution of the
  generators by Lie series, matrices or other objects with a
  user-supplied bracket, the Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff series
  and its symmetric version, exp(ad_A)B, and the Zassenhaus
  terms. It also supports computations in the Lie algebra of
  classical mechanics, the quotient of the free Lie algebra by
  the ideal generated by [B,[B,[B,A]]], through a generalized
  Hall basis based on the P-degree.
keywords:
  - free Lie algebra
  - Hall basis
  - Lyndon basis
  - Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff formula
  - Zassenhaus formula
  - Lie series
  - Lie algebra of classical mechanics
  - Mathematica
